+# Material Management + Profit Dashboard
+
+## Overview
+
+You want to unify **Work Types** (used in Rented Machinery) and **Materials** (used in Weighbridge) into a single entity — since they represent the same thing (Seawall, Baller, Quarry Waste, Muck, etc.). Each material/work-type will have a **rate per ton**. This enables profit calculation:
+
+- **Weighbridge Revenue** = Net Weight (tons) × Material Rate (₹/ton)
+- **Rented Cost** = Work Type Hours × Hourly Cost Rate (already exists)
+- **Profit** = Weighbridge Revenue − Rented Cost
+
+The profit dashboard is **admin-only** and shows daily, weekly, monthly breakdowns with a date range picker.
+
+---
+
+## Open Questions
+
+> [!IMPORTANT]
+> **Q1: Material rate — who sets it?**  
+> You said staff enters the material in the weighbridge form. But the material rate (₹/ton) — does admin set it globally in the Work Type/Material manager? Or does the **staff also enter the rate per trip**?
+> 
+> **Assumption**: Rate is set globally per material type by admin in the Material Manager dialog (same as the existing WorkType Manager). Staff only picks the material from the dropdown — they don't see or enter the rate.
+
+> [!IMPORTANT]
+> **Q2: Can staff see material dropdown in Weighbridge?**  
+> You said "staff can enter what material it is" — does this mean the **material dropdown IS visible to staff** in the Weighbridge page? And only the **rate and profit numbers** are hidden from staff?
+>
+> **Assumption**: Yes. Staff sees and fills the material dropdown in Weighbridge. Only the ₹ rate fields and profit dashboard are admin-only.
+
+> [!IMPORTANT]
+> **Q3: Does the Weighbridge "Remarks" field get REPLACED by the new "Material" dropdown?**  
+> Currently Weighbridge has a `remarks` field that already lists: baller, quarry waste, sea wall, muck. This is the same data as your new material dropdown.
+>
+> **Assumption**: Yes — the existing `remarks` dropdown in Weighbridge becomes the new **Material** dropdown, now pulling from the unified Material/Work Type API instead of a hardcoded list.
+
+> [!NOTE]
+> **Q4: Rented Work Type vs Material — same API?**  
+> Currently Work Types are stored separately. The plan is to make them the **same collection** with an added `ratePerTon` field. This means the Work Type Manager dialog will be updated to also accept a rate per ton, and will be accessible from **both** Rented Logs and Weighbridge pages.
+
+---
+
+## Proposed Changes
+
+### 1. Work Type / Material Unification (Backend API assumed unchanged, schema extended)
+
+The frontend will treat **Work Types** as **Materials** — the same entity, just with a new `ratePerTon` field.
+
+#### [MODIFY] [WorkTypeManagerDialog.jsx](file:///d:/Quarry/quarryFrontend/src/components/RentedMachinery/WorkTypeManagerDialog.jsx)
+- Rename title to **"Manage Materials / Work Types"**
+- Add a `ratePerTon` (₹/ton) input field alongside the name field
+- Show `ratePerTon` value in the list items
+- Send `ratePerTon` to the API when creating
+- This dialog is now shared — will also be accessible from Weighbridge page
+
+---
+
+### 2. Weighbridge Page Updates
+
+#### [MODIFY] [WeighbridgePage.jsx](file:///d:/Quarry/quarryFrontend/src/components/WeighbridgePage.jsx)
+
+**Material Field (Staff can see & fill):**
+- Replace the hardcoded `REMARKS_OPTIONS` / `remarks` field with a **Material** dropdown that fetches from the Work Types API (same as Rented uses)
+- Add a **"+ Add Custom Material"** button inline or in the dropdown that opens the `WorkTypeManagerDialog`
+- The field maps to `remarks` or a new `materialId` field in the API payload
+
+**Admin-only UI additions (hidden from staff):**
+- Show a small **₹ rate badge** next to the material name in the row — visible only to admin
+- Show calculated **Revenue per trip** = (netWeight / 1000) × ratePerTon — admin only
+
+**Column layout update:**
+- Add a "Material" column and optionally "Revenue" column (admin-only)
+
+**Stat cards update (admin-only):**
+- Add a "Weighbridge Revenue" stat card showing total revenue for the period
+
+---
+
+### 3. New Admin Profit Dashboard
+
+#### [NEW] `src/components/ProfitDashboard.jsx`
+
+A new page (admin-only) accessible from the **Dashboard** section. It includes:
+
+**Date Range Controls:**
+- Toggle: Daily / Weekly / Monthly
+- Custom date range picker
+
+**Revenue Section (from Weighbridge):**
+- Total net weight by material
+- Revenue = sum of (netWeight in tons × ratePerTon) per completed entry
+- Breakdown table by material type
+
+**Cost Section (from Rented Machinery):**
+- Total rented hours by work type
+- Cost = sum of (hours × hourly cost rate) per log
+- Breakdown table by work type / machine
+
+**Profit Summary Card:**
+- `Total Revenue − Total Rented Cost = Profit`
+- Color-coded: green for profit, red for loss
+- Period comparison badges (vs last period)
+
+**Chart (optional but recommended):**
+- Bar chart: Revenue vs Cost vs Profit by day/week/month
+- Material-wise revenue breakdown (pie or bar)
+
+---
+
+### 4. Admin Dashboard Route
+
+#### [MODIFY] [App.jsx](file:///d:/Quarry/quarryFrontend/src/App.jsx)
+- Add `case "Dashboard"` in `renderPage()` to render the new `ProfitDashboard` component
+- Currently the Dashboard case falls through to the default — fix this
+
+#### [MODIFY] [Layout.jsx](file:///d:/Quarry/quarryFrontend/src/components/Layout.jsx)
+- Dashboard is already `adminOnly: true` in the nav — no change needed here
+
+---
+
+### 5. Weighbridge + Rented — Access to Material Manager
+
+#### [MODIFY] [WeighbridgePage.jsx](file:///d:/Quarry/quarryFrontend/src/components/WeighbridgePage.jsx)
+- Import and use `WorkTypeManagerDialog` (renamed mentally as Material Manager)
+- Add a "Manage Materials" button in the header — only visible to admin
+
+---
+
+### 6. Hooks — Extend useWorkTypes
+
+#### [MODIFY] `src/hooks/useWorkTypes.js`  
+- Ensure `createWorkType` mutation sends `ratePerTon` field
+- The rest of the hook (fetch, delete) likely works as-is
+
+---
+
+## Data Flow Diagram
+
+```
+Material Manager (Admin sets: name + ratePerTon)
+     │
+     ├─► Rented Machinery: Work Type dropdown → hours × cost = rental cost
+     │
+     └─► Weighbridge: Material dropdown → netWeight(tons) × ratePerTon = revenue
+                                                     │
+                                     Profit Dashboard (Admin Only)
+                                     Revenue (Weighbridge) − Cost (Rented) = Profit
+```
+
+---
+
+## Role-Based Visibility Summary
+
+| Feature | Staff | Admin |
+|---|---|---|
+| Material dropdown in Weighbridge | ✅ Can select | ✅ Can select + manage |
+| Rate per ton in Material Manager | ❌ Hidden | ✅ Can set |
+| Revenue column in Weighbridge table | ❌ Hidden | ✅ Visible |
+| Revenue stat cards | ❌ Hidden | ✅ Visible |
+| Profit Dashboard page | ❌ Not in nav | ✅ Accessible |
+| Work Type dropdown in Rented | ✅ Can select | ✅ Can select + manage |
+
+---
+
+## Verification Plan
+
+### Manual Verification
+1. Log in as **staff** → Weighbridge page shows material dropdown, no rate/revenue info
+2. Log in as **admin** → Weighbridge shows revenue column and stat cards
+3. Admin navigates to **Dashboard** → Profit Dashboard renders with correct data
+4. Create a material from Work Type Manager with a rate → it appears in both Weighbridge and Rented dropdowns
+5. Complete a weighbridge entry → revenue is correctly computed
+6. Check Daily / Weekly / Monthly toggles in Profit Dashboard
